      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor\\), we first need to understand what the floor function \\(\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor\\) means. The floor function returns the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(x\\).\n\n1. **Identify the value of \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\):**\n   - \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\) is approximately \\(-1.6667\\).\n\n2. **Apply the floor function:**\n   - This means we are looking for the greatest integer that is less than or equal to \\(-1.6667\\).\n   - The integers are \\(\\ldots, -3, -2, -1, 0\\).\n\n3. **Determine the closest integer:**\n   - \\(-1.6667\\) falls between \\(-2\\) and \\(-1\\).\n   - Since the floor function returns the largest integer less than or equal to \\(-1.6667\\), we have:\n     \\[\n     \\left\\lfloor -1.6667 \\right\\rfloor = -2\n     \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = \\boxed{-2}\n   \\]",
