      "text": "To evaluate $\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor$, we need to first find the value of $-\\frac{5}{3}$. Since $5$ is $\\frac{1}{3}$ more than $4$, $-\\frac{5}{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3}$ less than $-4$. Therefore, $-\\frac{5}{3}$ is about $-4.333\\ldots$, a value which is less than $-4$. \n\nNow we need to use the floor function, which outputs the greatest integer not greater than the input value. The greatest and smallest integers not exceeding $-4.333\\ldots$ are $-4$: \n\n$$\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = -4.$$",
